    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d413">

                <pb facs="d413-01" n="1" xml:id="d413-01"/>

                <head>413. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                        (Kissinger) to Secretary
                    of State Rogers<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d413-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d413-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1972-03-28"
                        >March 28, 1972</date>
                </dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT:</label>
                    <item>Recognition of Bangladesh</item>
                </list>
                <p>In response to your memorandum of March 6, 1972, the President has decided that
                    U.S. recognition of Bangladesh should be announced at the Department of State
                    anytime after April 3.</p>
                <p>He has asked that cables be sent (1) immediately to Islamabad instructing our
                    Charge to inform President Bhutto, and
                    (2) to Paris instructing Ambassador to inform the PRC Ambassador. Every effort should be made to keep this move
                    confidential until the announcement is made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        Henry A. Kissinger
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d413-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d413-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files
                    1970–73, POL 16 BANGLADESH. Secret; Nodis.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d413-f2" n="2" xml:id="d413-f2-content">
                <p>
                    Kissinger informed Rogers that the President had decided that
                    United States recognition of Bangladesh should be announced at the Department of
                    State anytime after April 3.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
